cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "aqequiv: equivalence testing and sensor classification for ambient air quality measurements"
abstract: >-
  Python package, command-line tool and desktop application for the
  evaluation of parallel air quality measurements: equivalence of PM
  instruments with the reference method (EC Guide to the Demonstration of
  Equivalence, 2010; EN 16450:2017, including ongoing verification) and
  classification of sensor systems for PM and gases (CEN/TS 17660-1 and -2),
  with the Modified Target Diagram and the data quality objectives of
  Directive (EU) 2024/2881.
authors:
  - family-names: Borić
    given-names: Petar Krešimir
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24278513
repository-code: "https://github.com/pboric/aqequiv"
url: "https://github.com/pboric/aqequiv"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - air quality
  - particulate matter
  - equivalence
  - low-cost sensors
  - measurement uncertainty
  - orthogonal regression
  - CEN/TS 17660
  - EN 16450
